            "body": "@tjtanaa could you take a look when you have a moment? It's a small one, but on `main` right now `KVQuantMode.CUSTOM` is literally `OCTAVE_K3V4`, so any plugin dtype that returns `CUSTOM` goes down the Octave path. It came from #59774 and #52670 landing on the same day.\n\nBesides the fix, the enum is now `@unique`, so a repeated value fails at import instead of silently becoming an alias, and the sentinel test checks that `CUSTOM` doesn't read as any other mode. That way this can't happen again to whoever adds the next one.\n",
