    "body": "## Purpose\n\n`KVQuantMode.CUSTOM` and `KVQuantMode.OCTAVE_K3V4` share the value 12. #59774 (Octave KV) and #52670 (pluggable KV cache dtypes) landed the same day and each took the next free value. On an `IntEnum` a repeated value makes the second name an alias of the first, so on `main` today:\n\n```python\n>>> KVQuantMode.CUSTOM is KVQuantMode.OCTAVE_K3V4\nTrue\n>>> KVQuantMode.CUSTOM.is_octave\nTrue\n>>> get_kv_quant_mode(\"octave_k3v4\").is_custom_mode\nTrue\n```\n\nSo a registered dtype whose handler returns `CUSTOM` is treated as Octave by everything that checks `is_octave`, and `octave_k3v4` reports itself as a custom mode.\n\nThis PR moves `CUSTOM` to 15 and marks the enum `@unique`, so a future collision raises at import (`ValueError: duplicate values found in <enum 'KVQuantMode'>`) instead of creating a silent alias. Nothing persists these values, so renumbering is safe.\n\nNot a duplicate: no open PR touches `KVQuantMode` values (searched `KVQuantMode CUSTOM`, `OCTAVE_K3V4`).\n\n## Test Plan\n\n```bash\npytest -q tests/config/test_kv_cache_dtype.py\n```\n\n`test_backend_sentinel_properties` now also asserts that `CUSTOM` is neither TurboQuant nor Octave and that no other mode is a custom mode.\n\n## Test Result\n\n- With this PR: 6 passed.\n- With the old values (`CUSTOM = 12`, no `@unique`): `test_backend_sentinel_properties` fails at `assert mode.is_octave is False`.\n- With `@unique` and `CUSTOM = 12`: importing `vllm.v1.kv_cache_interface` raises `ValueError: duplicate values found in <enum 'KVQuantMode'>: CUSTOM -> OCTAVE_K3V4`.\n\nNo effect on model output for the built-in dtypes; only the value of the `CUSTOM` sentinel changes.\n\nAI assistance (Claude Code) was used to write this change; I reviewed every line and ran the tests above.\n\n\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63691?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795591490&installation_model_id=425286&pr_number=63691&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=vllm-project%2Fvllm&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fvllm-project%2Fvllm%2Fpull%2F63691&signature=4ed6f7e4deab7f6fcee4ddc24be90dc175a5ba2cc5f841662360559e89a4738f\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup>Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/vllm-project/codesmith/vllm/pr/63691?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-light-v3.svg\"><img alt=\"View with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/view-with-codesmith-dark-v3-3x.png\" width=\"162\" height=\"28\"></picture></a> <a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1795591500&installation_model_id=425286&pr_number